    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bcace970_1532282f",
        "filename": "pvmfw/avb/src/verify.rs",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 30,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-23T13:41:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Capabilities can be represented through the VBMeta properties in 2 ways:\n\n1. Have one property per capabilitiy e.g. `com.android.virt.cap.rpmb`, `com.android.virt.cap.mmu_on`, ... which is easy to parse but slightly larger in image size (negligible) and might not be consistent with libavb (do they use properties without values?)\n\n1. Have all of them in a single property:\n\n    - as a human-readable string (requires more parsing but more in-line with what seems to be done in existing VBMeta properties) e.g. `rpmb:mmu_on`\n    - as a bitfield represented as an unsigned value, which is the easiest to parse and as compact as possible, seems to be consistent with libavb given the existence of [`avb_property_lookup_uint64`](http://cs/android-internal/external/avb/libavb/avb_property_descriptor.h;l\u003d49;rcl\u003deeae447b7baf32568765801cb304d72dadfcd739), but isn\u0027t very user-friendly to `avbtool info_image` and friends.\n\n@jiyong@google.com, which one do we prefer?",
      "parentUuid": "7d55cff0_23766ceb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 29,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 30,
        "endChar": 12
      },
      "revId": "eebe294aaebc63aff20d1b7c3a48485fd41c038c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f3a7f478_8410cd53",
        "filename": "pvmfw/avb/src/verify.rs",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 30,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-23T15:26:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Option 1 is consistent with the way properties are currently set up in [core](http://cs/android-internal/build/make/core/Makefile;l\u003d4294;rcl\u003dd29e822310b591a9f46d4a0af4f57148ec971001) where each property takes a single value and it suits our current use case. I don\u0027t see anyone set up the property without value, I don\u0027t think it bothers so much to specify the vm_type here.\n\nIn the future, if someone wants to set up a group of similar properties, we can consider option 2. For example, if someone wants to pass a sets of public keys, they can add a property like\n```\n`com.android.virt.cap.pubkeys: \"key1|key2|...\"\n```",
      "parentUuid": "bcace970_1532282f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 29,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 30,
        "endChar": 12
      },
      "revId": "eebe294aaebc63aff20d1b7c3a48485fd41c038c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fc1935c9_dc3e3ab5",
        "filename": "rialto/Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 67,
