      "writtenOn": "2023-05-22T15:18:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Don\u0027t these VBMeta properties typically have a Java-like name, similar to Android system properties? For example, in the [core `Makefile`](http://cs/android-internal/build/make/core/Makefile;l\u003d4291;rcl\u003dd29e822310b591a9f46d4a0af4f57148ec971001), they use names such as\n```\ncom.android.build.$PART_NAME.{os_version,fingerprint,security_patch}\n```\nand IIRC, we already have an AVF namespace for system properties which could possibly be re-used here?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 67,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 67,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "eebe294aaebc63aff20d1b7c3a48485fd41c038c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
