    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "71f84db7_ca41ba7e",
        "filename": "rialto/Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 67,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-23T13:41:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not aware of any guidelines regarding naming these properties (please share if you manage to find some documentation!) but I\u0027d personally avoid re-using the `com.android.build` namespace and instead introduce our own (\"`com.android.virt`\"?) and would also re-using the property name \"`security_patch`\" as it has a very specific meaning under `com.android.build.$PART` (i.e. the date of the latest applied security patch) which wouldn\u0027t match what you want our new property to represent.\n\n@jiyong@google.com, our system properties use the namespace `hypervisor` (see [`CUSTOM_PVMFW_IMG_PATH_PROP`](http://cs/android/packages/modules/Virtualization/tests/hostside/java/com/android/microdroid/test/DebugPolicyHostTests.java;l\u003d70;rcl\u003d1b72e263c246e9bc991a2dd393622c59a9260c59), `CUSTOM_DEBUG_POLICY_PATH_PROP`, and [`KEY_METRICS_TAG`](http://cs/android/packages/modules/Virtualization/tests/helper/src/java/com/android/microdroid/test/common/DeviceProperties.java;l\u003d31;rcl\u003d1b72e263c246e9bc991a2dd393622c59a9260c59)), would that be preferred over \"`virt`\"?",
      "parentUuid": "8c851c38_0bdb02f5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 67,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 67,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "eebe294aaebc63aff20d1b7c3a48485fd41c038c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
